          "snippet": "The passages argue that possible-worlds semantics, rooted in Tarskian model theory and Carnap's work, provides a framework for evaluating truth conditions by relativizing them to specific worlds. This approach allows for the definition of objective modal notions and essential properties through quantification over sets of possible individuals and propositions. Furthermore, it enables actualist and haecceitist metaphysical interpretations to reinterpret these semantic structures while avoiding possibilism."
