          "snippet": "Gödel introduces various logical frameworks and consistency conditions, including ω-consistency for the First Incompleteness Theorem and well-orderings of variables to satisfy formulas. He demonstrates that non-standard models arise from completeness and compactness in Peano Arithmetic, while also establishing a definable well-ordering within the constructible universe L to support the Axiom of Choice. Additionally, he explores speed-up phenomena across higher-type systems and formalizes absoluteness through satisfaction predicates."
