          "snippet": "Kant advances the claim that he has provided a complete solution to Hume's problem regarding causality by distinguishing between strict and comparative universality. He supports this assertion through his analysis in the Second Analogy, where he links these distinctions to Hume’s discussion of necessary connection while clarifying that their relationship is not deductive."
